rd/ContinueReadingRow inline card) uses a CSS-only hover lift — typically `transform: translateY(-2px)` plus a border-color shift under a `transition: transform var(--transition-fast)` rule. Reveal animation today is a GSAP `gsap.from(cards, { opacity, y, stagger })` triggered once per row by ExpandableSection / CardGrid via useGSAP + ScrollTrigger (see ExpandableSection.tsx lines 30–53 and CardGrid.tsx lines 16–37). There is NO mousemove / proximity hover effect anywhere yet — cards animate only on their own :hover and on scroll-into-view.","integrationPoints":"There are five distinct row/grid container DOM nodes that hold cards as direct children — these are the natural mousemove listeners (each card is `containerRef.current.children[i]`, matching the existing GSAP stagger pattern). (1) ExpandableSection.tsx — `<div ref={containerRef} className={expanded ? styles.expanded : styles.row}>{children}</div>` (lines 77–82). Used by RecommendationsRow, RelatedSection, and three Browse rails (New Stories / New Series + the Most Liked / Most Read / Author's Choice rails via HomepageItem). The same containerRef toggles between flex row (`.row`) and grid (`.expanded`) — both are valid dock contexts. (2) CardGrid.tsx — `<div ref={containerRef} className={styles.grid}>{children}</div>` (lines 42–45). Used by /search and /tag/[slug] for the Stories and Series grid sections. (3) ContinueReadingRow.tsx — `<ul className={styles.list}>` with `<li>` direct children wrapping `<Link className={styles.card}>` (lines 34–49). No useRef yet — would need to add one. (4) ResumeReadingRow.tsx — `<ul className={styles.list}>` with `<li>` direct children wrapping `<ContinueCard>` (lines 90–96). Shares ContinueReadingRow.module.css. No useRef yet. (5) app/page.tsx hero `<div className={styles.heroCardsList}>` (lines 72–76) — flex-column of 3 SeriesCards rendered server-side; would need extraction into a tiny client wrapper to attach a ref. The cleanest single hook point is to add a generic ProximityRow / useDockProximity hook applied inside the existing containerRef effect in ExpandableSection + CardGrid + ContinueReadingRow + ResumeReadingRow + a new wrapper on the homepage hero — all share the "ref on container, children are the cards" shape, which is exactly what a GSAP mousemove → distance-to-center → scale transform needs. The cards themselves carry `data-tag-ids` already so adding scale/translate via GSAP `gsap.set(card, { scale, y })` per-frame won't conflict with the existing CSS `transition: transform`-driven hover lift — but be aware of that interaction: the proximity scale and the CSS `:hover { transform: translateY(-2px) }` both write to `transform`, so either move CSS lift into the GSAP timeline or use `gsap.quickTo` with `translate3d`/`scale` while disabling the CSS hover transform on cards inside a proximity-enabled row.","notes":"Row / grid containers that wrap cards on the PUBLIC site: ExpandableSection (`.row` flex / `.expanded` grid — used on /browse, RecommendationsRow, RelatedSection on /story|/series|/chapter); CardGrid (`.grid` auto-fill grid — used on /search and /tag/[slug]); ContinueReadingRow `.list` (flex row of <li>); ResumeReadingRow `.list` (flex row of <li> wrapping ContinueCard, reuses ContinueReadingRow.module.css); homepage hero `.heroCardsList` (vertical flex of 3 SeriesCards in app/page.tsx). Public-site card-rendering page surfaces: `/` (SeriesCard x3 in hero), `/browse` (ResumeReadingRow + ContinueReadingRow + RecommendationsRow + 5 ExpandableSection rails with StoryCard / SeriesCard / HomepageItem), `/search` (CardGrid of StoryCard + CardGrid of SeriesCard), `/tag/[slug]` (CardGrid of StoryCard + CardGrid of SeriesCard), `/story/[id]` (RelatedSection → ExpandableSection of StoryCard|SeriesCard), `/chapter/[id]` (RelatedSection → ExpandableSection of StoryCard|SeriesCard), `/series/[id]` (RelatedSection → ExpandableSection of StoryCard|SeriesCard; plus ChapterList — vertical row list, separate question whether dock e